    "description": "Every HTTP API of [Octane](https://octane.wtf). Generated from the website's own code with Swashbuckle, so the list is complete; response examples come from the live site.\n\n## Sites and URLs\n\nLike Roblox, the APIs live on subdomains: `users.octane.wtf`, `catalog.octane.wtf` and so on. Each method shows its real URL.\n\nEvery subdomain API also answers on the main domain under `/apisite/<name>/`, for example `https://users.octane.wtf/v1/users/1` = `https://octane.wtf/apisite/users/v1/users/1`. The paths on this page use that form, so **Test Request** works right from this page.\n\n| Site | Methods |\n|---|---|\n| `octane.wtf` | 125 |\n| `abtesting.octane.wtf` | 4 |\n| `accountinformation.octane.wtf` | 14 |\n| `accountsettings.octane.wtf` | 22 |\n| `ads.octane.wtf` | 5 |\n| `api.octane.wtf` | 34 |\n| `apis.octane.wtf` | 30 |\n| `assetdelivery.octane.wtf` | 4 |\n| `assetgame.octane.wtf` | 20 |\n| `auth.octane.wtf` | 16 |\n| `avatar.octane.wtf` | 31 |\n| `badges.octane.wtf` | 7 |\n| `billing.octane.wtf` | 1 |\n| `catalog.octane.wtf` | 24 |\n| `chat.octane.wtf` | 19 |\n| `client-telemetry.octane.wtf` | 2 |\n| `clientsettingscdn.octane.wtf` | 2 |\n| `contacts.octane.wtf` | 3 |\n| `data.octane.wtf` | 3 |\n| `develop.octane.wtf` | 72 |\n| `donations.octane.wtf` | 7 |\n| `economy.octane.wtf` | 21 |\n| `ecsv2.octane.wtf` | 21 |\n| `followings.octane.wtf` | 4 |\n| `friends.octane.wtf` | 20 |\n| `gameinternationalization.octane.wtf` | 16 |\n| `gamejoin.octane.wtf` | 3 |\n| `games.octane.wtf` | 25 |\n| `groups.octane.wtf` | 62 |\n| `inventory.octane.wtf` | 7 |\n| `itemconfiguration.octane.wtf` | 9 |\n| `locale.octane.wtf` | 4 |\n| `metrics.octane.wtf` | 4 |\n| `notifications.octane.wtf` | 7 |\n| `premiumfeatures.octane.wtf` | 3 |\n| `presence.octane.wtf` | 2 |\n| `privatemessages.octane.wtf` | 11 |\n| `publish.octane.wtf` | 3 |\n| `realtime.octane.wtf` | 8 |\n| `textfilter.octane.wtf` | 3 |\n| `thumbnails.octane.wtf` | 11 |\n| `trades.octane.wtf` | 8 |\n| `translationroles.octane.wtf` | 1 |\n| `twostepverification.octane.wtf` | 1 |\n| `users.octane.wtf` | 11 |\n\n## Authentication\n\n- **Login** is the `.ROBLOSECURITY` cookie that octane.wtf sets after you sign in. **Test Request** sends it automatically when you are logged in on the site.\n- **CSRF.** Every `POST`, `PATCH` and `DELETE` needs the `x-csrf-token` header. Send the request without it: the API answers `403` with an `x-csrf-token` response header. Repeat the request with that value. A token lives about 5 minutes.\n\n## Errors\n\nErrors use the Roblox format:\n\n```json\n{\"errors\": [{\"code\": 0, \"message\": \"Unauthorized\"}]}\n```\n\n`401` means you are not logged in, `403` with \"Token Validation Failed\" means a missing or old CSRF token, `429` means too many requests.\n\n## Limits\n\nRequests are limited per IP; over the limit the API answers `429`. Some methods (login, sign-up, purchases) have their own stricter limits.\n"
